0M17273 2576h0M19111 3007h0M18470 1607h0M11936 2066h0M12537 1310h0M12411 1613h0M12168 1689h0M12806 1120h0M12703 1200h0M12682 1268h0M12852 1984h0M13280 5526h0M12670 4873h0M12761 4972h0M12636 5052h0M12574 5201h0M12582 5313h0M12971 1242h0M13063 1112h0M13015 1059h0M12954 1083h0M12577 1419h0M12654 1408h0M13063 1112h0M11924 1823h0M11924 1823h0M12506 1728h0M18828 2012h0M18464 4874h0M19119 4624h0M18648 5524h0M6264 3376h0M6965 3761h0M7073 3840h0M7239 3762h0M7387 3898h0M7808 4236h0M8148 3441h0M7430 3075h0M7246 1660h0M7178 1510h0M6064 1862h0M1034 6767h0M19378 7831h0M13316 1127h0M13549 991h0M13634 1222h0M14132 950h0M14132 950h0M13210 953h0M13406 760h0M13574 785h0M13831 749h0M13790 781h0M13650 893h0M13565 976h0M16906 2722h0M17212 2740h0M17193 3122h0M16490 3538h0M16404 4277h0M16073 2962h0M18579 3612h0M18602 4082h0M10973 4526h0M10701 3759h0M10678 4461h0"/></svg><figcaption><span class="map-key"><i class="k-p"></i>Profile</span><span class="map-key"><i class="k-s"></i>State</span><span>658 states with a known seat in 1939</span><a href="/atlas?year=1939">Open the atlas at 1939 &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-finland"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Finland.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Finland</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Soviet Union attacks, starting the Winter War</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-yugoslavia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Yugoslavia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Yugoslavia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Cvetković-Maček Agreement creates the Banovina of Croatia</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/czechoslovakia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Czechoslovakia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Czechoslovakia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Germany occupies Bohemia and Moravia; Slovakia becomes a separate state</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/nazi-germany"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Nazi%20Germany.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Nazi Germany</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Germany invades Poland on 1 September, starting the Second World War in Europe</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/manchukuo"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Manchukuo.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Manchukuo</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A border skirmish between Manchukuoan and Mongolian cavalry in May escalates into the Battles of Khalkhin Gol, where a Soviet–Mongolian force defeats the Kwantung Army.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/mandatory-palestine"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mandatory%20Palestine.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mandatory Palestine</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The revolt ends in March with more than 5,000 Arabs, 400 Jews and 200 British dead; the White Paper restricts Jewish immigration and land purchase and promises an independent state within ten years.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/aboriginal-australians"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Aboriginal%20Australians.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Aboriginal Australians</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">About 200 people leave Cummeragunja Station in protest at their treatment, in the Cummeragunja walk-off</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/may-fourth-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/May%20Fourth%20Movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>May Fourth Movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Mao Zedong calls the May Fourth Movement a new stage in China’s bourgeois-democratic revolution</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/fascism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Fascism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Fascism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Germany invades Poland, beginning World War II, in which the Axis powers carry out the Holocaust</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-lithuania-1918-1940"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Lithuania%20(1918-1940).png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Lithuania (1918-1940)</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Lithuania cedes the Klaipėda Region to Germany and receives Vilnius under the Soviet–Lithuanian Mutual Assistance Pact</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/francoist-spain"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Francoist%20Spain.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Francoist Spain</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Nationalists win the Spanish Civil War, and the Falange is declared the sole legally sanctioned party</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/korea-under-japanese-rule"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Korea%20under%20Japanese%20rule.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Korea under Japanese rule</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Recruitment of Korean labour for Japan begins, and the Sōshi-kaimei decrees press Koreans to give up their clan-based family names</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/second-polish-republic"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Second%20Polish%20Republic.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Second Polish Republic</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Germany and Slovakia invade on 1 September and the Soviet Union on 17 September, and organised resistance ends on 6 October after the Battle of Kock</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/second-spanish-republic"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Second%20Spanish%20Republic.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Second Spanish Republic</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Madrid falls in March, and the Republic is dissolved after surrendering to the Nationalists</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battles-of-khalkhin-gol"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battles%20of%20Khalkhin%20Gol.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battles of Khalkhin Gol</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A Mongolian cavalry unit is driven back across the Khalkhin Gol by Manchukoan cavalry</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battles-of-khalkhin-gol"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battles%20of%20Khalkhin%20Gol.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battles of Khalkhin Gol</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Zhukov opens his offensive with artillery and 557 aircraft</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battles-of-khalkhin-gol"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battles%20of%20Khalkhin%20Gol.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battles of Khalkhin Gol</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Soviet Union and Japan agree a cease-fire</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/prague"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Prague.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Prague</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">German forces enter Prague, and Bohemia and Moravia become a protectorate</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/krakow"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Krak%C3%B3w.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kraków</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Kraków becomes the capital of the General Government under Nazi Germany</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/madurai"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Madurai.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Madurai</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The temple entry movement is first led at the Meenakshi Temple</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/quit-india-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Quit%20India%20movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Quit India movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">India is brought into the war without consultation, and the Congress ministers of eight provinces resign</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/rastafari"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Rastafari.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Rastafari</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Howell forms a Rasta community known as Pinnacle in Saint Catherine Parish, which the police raid repeatedly and which closes in 1954</span></li></ul></section>
